        <mxCell id="r19" value="&lt;b&gt;Scoring radar&lt;/b&gt; (illustrative values, one card)" style="text;html=1;align=left;fontSize=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20.0" y="20.0" width="800" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="r20" value="&lt;font color='#b85450'&gt;&lt;b&gt;solid red&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;: base CV&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color='#82b366'&gt;&lt;b&gt;dashed green&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;: CV after the Lift edits&lt;br&gt;gap between them = Lift" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="870.0" y="120.0" width="260" height="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="r21" value="&lt;b&gt;Before the chart: knockouts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Only the user's own hard preferences and facts the posting states outright (no sponsorship, a required language). Unknown passes and becomes a question.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Scale on every axis&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;3 done and shown on the record&lt;br&gt;2 transferable: same activity under the same constraints, only the domain or tool differs&lt;br&gt;1 gap the user closes in days or weeks&lt;br&gt;0 gap of months: the activity itself was never done&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;What tailoring can move&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Quick scan, must-haves and nice-to-haves, by surfacing what the record already holds. Never Want.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Tier&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;A: both Want axes high and tailored shape high. Tailored CV and letter, same day&lt;br&gt;B: Want high and base shape good, or Want lower and shape high. Base CV&lt;br&gt;C: Want low, or any must-have at 0. Kept on the board with the reason" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;spacing=6;strokeColor=#CCCCCC;rounded=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="870.0" y="200.0" width="280" height="420" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
